<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Raspberry Pi on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/raspberry-pi/</link><description>Recent content in Raspberry Pi on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2020 11:37:44 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/raspberry-pi/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Apple Pi Os</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/applepi/</link><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2020 11:37:44 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/applepi/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Interesting looking Pi Os&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen" loading="eager" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/nxL_zVywEnU?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0" style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;" title="YouTube video"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Building Raspberry PI image using Vagrant</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/building-raspberry-pi-image-using/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Dec 2016 09:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/building-raspberry-pi-image-using/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Building your own Raspberry Pi Images&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjVG_n8KUxrSA1GvKJRMktj_YDDC5AHFZ331zBaaRvndeaL6TtDnlsnPc-PzYYKhlRDipiBQvBFsfJku0GmF6Quqc_tE25IJX-4UtOBXWcmijnFdGET-vV7rvfSotDRH5Ea5boHEvBFAqQ/s1600/raspberrypi2.jpg" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="181" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjVG_n8KUxrSA1GvKJRMktj_YDDC5AHFZ331zBaaRvndeaL6TtDnlsnPc-PzYYKhlRDipiBQvBFsfJku0GmF6Quqc_tE25IJX-4UtOBXWcmijnFdGET-vV7rvfSotDRH5Ea5boHEvBFAqQ/s320/raspberrypi2.jpg" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;The Vagrant file on &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pibuild"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pibuild&lt;/a&gt; sets up a build environment for building Raspberry Pi images from the repository &lt;a href="https://github.com/RPi-Distro/pi-gen"&gt;https://github.com/RPi-Distro/pi-gen&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;I am using it to create a custom image minimal with &lt;a href="https://www.docker.com/"&gt;Docker&lt;/a&gt; pre-installed based on &lt;a href="https://github.com/jonasrosland/pi-gen"&gt;https://github.com/jonasrosland/pi-gen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;although you can edit the scripts to pre-install the packages you want in your image.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Make a Raspberry Pi Portable Arcade Console (with Retropie)</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/make-raspberry-pi-portable-arcade/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Aug 2016 09:10:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/make-raspberry-pi-portable-arcade/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Looks like a cool project without doing a full arcade machine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="270" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bYHXUECdQAg" width="480"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>No static external IP on Raspberry Pi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/no-static-external-ip-on-raspberry-pi/</link><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jan 2014 14:07:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/no-static-external-ip-on-raspberry-pi/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;My Internet provider doesn't supply me with a static IP address with my broadband, so my Raspberry Pi external web address can wander if my router or connectigets reset. There are third party sites which will provide you with a static URL which follows your wandering IP address but its fun to do it yourself.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;To keep me updated on the current IP I wrote a Ruby script which I run via crontab to check and Tweet me is the IP address changes.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre style="color: #333333; font-family: Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Courier, monospace; font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px;"&gt;&lt;div class="line" id="LC1" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="c1" style="color: #999988; font-style: italic;"&gt;#!/usr/bin/ruby&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC2" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="nb" style="color: #0086b3;"&gt;require&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'open-uri'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC3" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="nb" style="color: #0086b3;"&gt;require&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'twitter'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC4" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC5" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="n"&gt;twitDM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"twitter_username"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC6" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC7" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="n"&gt;remote_ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb" style="color: #0086b3;"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'http://whatismyip.akamai.com'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC8" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="n"&gt;old_ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no" style="color: teal;"&gt;File&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'remote_ip.txt'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'r'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC9" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC10" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;remote_ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;old_ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC11" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="no" style="color: teal;"&gt;File&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;'remote_ip.txt'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"w"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;write&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;remote_ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC12" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC13" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no" style="color: teal;"&gt;Twitter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no" style="color: teal;"&gt;REST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no" style="color: teal;"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC14" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;consumer_key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"xxxx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC15" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;consumer_secret&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"xxxx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC16" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;access_token&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"xxxx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC17" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;access_token_secret&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"xxxx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC18" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC19" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC20" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"D &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;#{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;twitDM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt; My IP address is now &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;#{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;remote_ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC21" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC22" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC23" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="nb" style="color: #0086b3;"&gt;puts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2" style="color: #dd1144;"&gt;"IP addresses match"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="line" id="LC24" style="padding-left: 10px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span class="k" style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;You can clone the script at Github&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/myip"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/myip&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;it uses a Ruby Twitter API library which can be found at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://github.com/sferik/twitter"&gt;https://github.com/sferik/twitter&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to do the direct message with the new IP.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Full details about getting your Twitter API keys can be found at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://dev.twitter.com/"&gt;https://dev.twitter.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>HDMIPi Affordable 9" High-Def screen for the Raspberry Pi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/hdmipi-affordable-9-high-def-screen-for/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Nov 2013 11:53:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/hdmipi-affordable-9-high-def-screen-for/</guid><description>&lt;iframe width="480" height="360" src="http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/697708033/hdmipi-affordable-9-high-def-screen-for-the-raspbe/widget/video.html" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"&gt; &lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;Looks like a good project to back for a Raspberry Pi HD screen.&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/697708033/hdmipi-affordable-9-high-def-screen-for-the-raspbe?mc_cid=0c18ad0bb5&amp;amp;mc_eid=e3dfdcb9ad"&gt;HDMIPi Affordable 9" High-Def screen for the Raspberry Pi by Alex Eames - RasPi.TV — Kickstarter&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;</description></item><item><title>Tiny Tiny RSS Part 2</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/tiny-tiny-rss-part-2/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Jul 2013 09:51:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/tiny-tiny-rss-part-2/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Installed the clean looking &lt;a href="https://github.com/asyncopation/ttrss-theme-chalk" target="_blank"&gt;Chalk Theme&lt;/a&gt; on my &lt;a href="http://tt-rss.org/redmine/projects/tt-rss/wiki" target="_blank"&gt;Tiny Tiny RSS server&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;running on my &lt;a href="http://www.raspberrypi.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Raspberry Pi&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg-wK_4lm384Y8S0euxwmtbjZnptwSGOOeK-y2htkvfTrWRP0jE1dRPYvoxacmqi4KKhYw-UHfCQ8Nqi66CDblrjAr2fTceAQydxxtxC3eAR9rWAy3k7oII-t-Yt92alzoZSmKgaiPyBHw/s1600/Clipboard-1.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="260" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg-wK_4lm384Y8S0euxwmtbjZnptwSGOOeK-y2htkvfTrWRP0jE1dRPYvoxacmqi4KKhYw-UHfCQ8Nqi66CDblrjAr2fTceAQydxxtxC3eAR9rWAy3k7oII-t-Yt92alzoZSmKgaiPyBHw/s320/Clipboard-1.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Tiny Tiny RSS</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/tiny-tiny-rss/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Jun 2013 11:49:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/tiny-tiny-rss/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="font-size: 0.8em; line-height: 1.6em; margin: 0 0 10px 0; padding: 0;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/9158795086/" title="Tiny Tiny RSS"&gt;&lt;img alt="Tiny Tiny RSS by Alastair Montgomery" src="http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3784/9158795086_28c0c7db2e.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="margin: 0;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/9158795086/"&gt;Tiny Tiny RSS&lt;/a&gt;, a photo by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt; on Flickr.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;Running Tiny Tiny RSS News Feed reader on my Raspberry Pi.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Setup on Lighttpd and MySQL using the instructions on &lt;a href="http://tt-rss.org/redmine/projects/tt-rss/wiki"&gt;http://tt-rss.org/redmine/projects/tt-rss/wiki&lt;/a&gt; as a replacement to Google Reader.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Working well so far.&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspbmc</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspbmc/</link><pubDate>Mon, 27 May 2013 16:36:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspbmc/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Got my second Raspberry Pi setup as a media center with Raspbmc.&lt;br&gt;&#10;Wifi setup was painless just a case of connecting it and entering the wifi connection details.&lt;br&gt;&#10;Just need a new powered USB hub as the power supply died on the one I've got.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class='separator' style='clear: both; text-align: center;'&gt; &lt;a href='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhAw02noODnjiPbJ0o0if2nVi7giKQE4c8hFGnAkpoWjyUxrrHqCKTowC7myTF-T5RDaSzJ_YnBLd95XA6FQyXLNGpsLk58PUCnH1ojRgNMUGq4IhdpyctppCZ4iWXPHyhzp_dgSS-YJbk/s1600/2013-05-27_13-23-31_62.jpg' imageanchor='1' style='margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;'&gt; &lt;img border='0' src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhAw02noODnjiPbJ0o0if2nVi7giKQE4c8hFGnAkpoWjyUxrrHqCKTowC7myTF-T5RDaSzJ_YnBLd95XA6FQyXLNGpsLk58PUCnH1ojRgNMUGq4IhdpyctppCZ4iWXPHyhzp_dgSS-YJbk/s640/2013-05-27_13-23-31_62.jpg' /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class='separator' style='clear: both; text-align: center;'&gt; &lt;a href='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiXaFCB5FOdJxYcegga6g-5eYwBO-adaiXekRKr8Hxt1TFFaN3Cb1Ge9NchUPMY7Z8JjythD8BSgaj4dfmkCrI367LBXDAy0wDQtjTYJYAGeXUbcaVei40D4fmWYrMBwGZ45M0p1p57xeU/s1600/2013-05-27_13-30-04_332.jpg' imageanchor='1' style='margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;'&gt; &lt;img border='0' src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiXaFCB5FOdJxYcegga6g-5eYwBO-adaiXekRKr8Hxt1TFFaN3Cb1Ge9NchUPMY7Z8JjythD8BSgaj4dfmkCrI367LBXDAy0wDQtjTYJYAGeXUbcaVei40D4fmWYrMBwGZ45M0p1p57xeU/s640/2013-05-27_13-30-04_332.jpg' /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Piwigo Instance Live</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-piwigo-instance-live/</link><pubDate>Fri, 26 Apr 2013 10:43:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-piwigo-instance-live/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;I've finally got my Piwigo instance running on my Raspberry Pi live to the internet &lt;a href="http://alastairhm.no-ip.org/piwigo/"&gt;http://alastairhm.no-ip.org/piwigo/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgd_A38WUOc0HGbquOEN6GlrlU_JmgJH_LYNROq3XuXf0G2g_GQvFaiFpD-8RYwUxaD_a-0tts17sav4tS2-PHlxYq6aq1FPygZB0qEW77PiBC1dyvSCcvaedG4yxjCF80lCl7Oi8BKWgs/s1600/raspberry-pi-web.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="240" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgd_A38WUOc0HGbquOEN6GlrlU_JmgJH_LYNROq3XuXf0G2g_GQvFaiFpD-8RYwUxaD_a-0tts17sav4tS2-PHlxYq6aq1FPygZB0qEW77PiBC1dyvSCcvaedG4yxjCF80lCl7Oi8BKWgs/s320/raspberry-pi-web.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgm2xZldbL0BrhaCIrHLeGbV0Yah4iCi4Lu3VFPvdBRwuzGFepkxlbHL6qC06be-V3wwUA7jQqggnrb1JgwJCmRvE1UAKpOQkPPZDHnoyMZWa0UXDYrU2jP91AesJ378xdy_mqw5AHSFoQ/s1600/raspberry-pi-web2.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="320" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgm2xZldbL0BrhaCIrHLeGbV0Yah4iCi4Lu3VFPvdBRwuzGFepkxlbHL6qC06be-V3wwUA7jQqggnrb1JgwJCmRvE1UAKpOQkPPZDHnoyMZWa0UXDYrU2jP91AesJ378xdy_mqw5AHSFoQ/s320/raspberry-pi-web2.png" width="262" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;It is running on Lighttpd and mySQL.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Media Center</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-media-center/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Apr 2013 09:58:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-media-center/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10;I had a quick look at the openELEC (&lt;a href="http://openelec.tv/" target="_blank"&gt; http://openelec.tv/&lt;/a&gt;)&amp;nbsp; media center for the Raspberry Pi last night using Berryboot ( &lt;a href="http://www.berryterminal.com/doku.php/berryboot"&gt;http://www.berryterminal.com/doku.php/berryboot&lt;/a&gt; ) to install it along side Debian on my card.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10;Looks pretty good, lots of plugins you can install to be able to access online content like 4oD and YouTube.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10;Might need to buy another Pi for the front room :)&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Setting up Piwigo on Raspberry Pi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/setting-up-piwigo-on-raspberry-pi/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Apr 2013 23:20:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/setting-up-piwigo-on-raspberry-pi/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Installed the gallery software &lt;a href="http://piwigo.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Piwigo&lt;/a&gt; on my Raspberry Pi, screenshots below.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;After installing lighttpd and MySQL5 and the other &lt;a href="http://piwigo.org/basics/requirements" target="_blank"&gt;prerequisites&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;you can install it using&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-family: Courier New, Courier, monospace;"&gt;sudo apt-get install piwigo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Although this is an older version, if you want the latest you'll need to go through the &lt;a href="http://piwigo.org/basics/installation_manual" target="_blank"&gt;manual installation route&lt;/a&gt; which is detailed on their web page.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;On my Ubuntu desktop, I did a trial run updating the version installed with apt-get using the Piwigo's internal upgrade option but this failed so might not be a viable option. &lt;a href="http://piwigo.org/basics/upgrade" target="_blank"&gt;More upgrade information here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiw91T8NxoN1abqAFuCxcjYg3yzk9Z_DgT-JReCvACYAsLrEhqXsOk4q1nejSXgOPtqGrBuZK4Gob2ySN6eyjnnSKNVQbYmV_WIeCSiPkLTIjvLwVwW-MbR9mUbwjG5FWFPf1lviXiYR98/s1600/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:13:09.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="200" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiw91T8NxoN1abqAFuCxcjYg3yzk9Z_DgT-JReCvACYAsLrEhqXsOk4q1nejSXgOPtqGrBuZK4Gob2ySN6eyjnnSKNVQbYmV_WIeCSiPkLTIjvLwVwW-MbR9mUbwjG5FWFPf1lviXiYR98/s320/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:13:09.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;Setting Up&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhInyiCqYO9bVpKXuAdxOxgozV0ijkbRzilgoC_9Nv9FIolkkRAxd6re__rLzwXVTN7WOL-XO2CSECRf0xeUPQokRPACYg0ti6_-lQ76Nk0r9gdNoIs1DHOf8ESdcZ7KwxHkxToGmiJD-0/s1600/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:15:53.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="250" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhInyiCqYO9bVpKXuAdxOxgozV0ijkbRzilgoC_9Nv9FIolkkRAxd6re__rLzwXVTN7WOL-XO2CSECRf0xeUPQokRPACYg0ti6_-lQ76Nk0r9gdNoIs1DHOf8ESdcZ7KwxHkxToGmiJD-0/s400/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:15:53.png" width="400" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;External access from Internet using No-Ip, you'll need to configure your router to pass HTTP requests to the Raspberry Pi.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjbatDU8zRc3aiCwGFc-asuCaUvCDUvbLXqhJqpBe9Yw7huOLtgyxC2nqhvFceVI5G9rcQtTWXRm6YUeUAlWwqdcnlA8BQJvFgnK32uto5AfOrlOTWPXjdcPdi9UWDCa9bEQ8SM48I9q-o/s1600/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:14:33.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="200" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjbatDU8zRc3aiCwGFc-asuCaUvCDUvbLXqhJqpBe9Yw7huOLtgyxC2nqhvFceVI5G9rcQtTWXRm6YUeUAlWwqdcnlA8BQJvFgnK32uto5AfOrlOTWPXjdcPdi9UWDCa9bEQ8SM48I9q-o/s320/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+23:14:33.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;Local network access from Ubuntu desktop.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Lighttpd running on my Raspberry Pi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-running-on-my-raspberry-pi/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Apr 2013 22:02:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-running-on-my-raspberry-pi/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Finally got round to playing a bit more with my Raspberry Pi, got Lighttpd installed on it, just a case of running;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-family: Courier New, Courier, monospace;"&gt;sudo apt-get install lighttpd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Although I had to create the &lt;b&gt;www-data&lt;/b&gt; group manually before this would install successfully.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;More details can be found on&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjl5ALTHtND-uw5FE2NS1rWaI2tMrA9KLWMsKbmpiUrudgKdBy8DIEaWjZc1-gKWX-MmfJ8yh1v3WvAex7Kewdbw-kTrivXkTdO5NK9CV-kf-qAdZK_Ytvgnjg2EUSQUSx2VV3yF3KYJiY/s1600/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+21:51:44.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="400" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjl5ALTHtND-uw5FE2NS1rWaI2tMrA9KLWMsKbmpiUrudgKdBy8DIEaWjZc1-gKWX-MmfJ8yh1v3WvAex7Kewdbw-kTrivXkTdO5NK9CV-kf-qAdZK_Ytvgnjg2EUSQUSx2VV3yF3KYJiY/s640/Screenshot+from+2013-04-10+21:51:44.png" width="640" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi in case</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-in-case/</link><pubDate>Wed, 27 Jun 2012 17:53:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-in-case/</guid><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;My Raspberry Pi in a case from piworks.Co.uk&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEj96HKIbHmoQb0JnL1qZRQu011o8ia0lItuhZrQNmJecfR7equhhaUzC25c0EUBgbEfuKJDkG3iSWTJMhFuz4AcsKm_CBn_694G67W1SkuK3hPTVivrD8g3G5FnovVouQVajCZp/' /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>First boot</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/first-boot/</link><pubDate>Sat, 23 Jun 2012 15:13:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/first-boot/</guid><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://instagr.am/p/MOCHVnN-hg/"&gt;http://instagr.am/p/MOCHVnN-hg/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;First boot of my Raspberry Pi.&lt;br&gt;&#10;Feel like I'm ten again sat in front of the TV with my Acorn Electron&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg-F5FJ231frlXNc-_GeKt8cHHJn5YyVrrKy_vnpDipeyLiq5rsF2rkbxXL8GLV_WxHYaRXNpYpww-n9x7n-ExY_x9oRctyTvTuWT3xaw_xDw0Gjsb4wKIGV2NyK8KSJXyqG3OSeqxPaQI/' /&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgSsoJGzOEwEEiXs7_Oxyp8_uthaxtlIYy9MxFU2oEhR4wbSQVeNa0Hje9-XfpbogbG9Lw4J-CZOYvTGnhri0zbu40ySr5FdVQRTe59hdb-5X807ptuPizGMui0E6KpMQUo-cx65Yv4hwE/' /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi SD Card problems</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-sd-card-problems/</link><pubDate>Mon, 11 Jun 2012 11:41:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-sd-card-problems/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Raspberry Cry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Was going to fire up my Raspberry Pi for the first time yesterday but had issues creating boot SD card for it on Windows 7. As you can see here from my post at the &lt;a href="http://www.raspberrypi.org/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?f=26&amp;amp;t=8020&amp;amp;p=96362#p96362"&gt;Pi Forum&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Looks like it was either problems with my desktop or the SD Card reader I was using as it was getting write errors when using the two Windows methods of creating the boot image.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Hopefully I can get the SD card reformat with GParted so I can try again, most annoying that I tripped up at the first hurdle.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi unwrapped</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-unwrapped/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Jun 2012 18:15:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-unwrapped/</guid><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It finally arrived, my Raspberry Pi, lots of geeky fun awaits.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Can't believe how small it is :)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjyGbc10j_muoivVu0s0GbNVtpPojkmAJfi48-0_w1m8ltNOqwCtaIhtMdBtl_GqGVEkBbKmxs87WgvCB8PLMr4jlgmfvXCsrBVNIuBCC9PhdhbJDgZzOxFckAbSJcmV8e8qmfa4JlfLTk/' /&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjrznicWBsjwv2GxzbchwUnqQEkdWggZtSZQd_bJ8hxoSsc_s_ck0gy6alDE012B7nPvayKronSYDQA5nLGZQFXGWyFpcVTQPXTQM5HX0q0yHpciHbc-rdGVeqyR6AMS3R6BfahQ7Cankw/' /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>